---
import CodeBlock from "../../components/ui/CodeBlock.astro";
import ModelSection from "../../components/models/ModelSection.astro";
import ModelLayout from "../../layouts/ModelLayout.astro";
import { sectionLookup } from "../../lib/models";

const sections = [
  {
    id: "how-they-work-together",
    title: "How they work together",
  },
  {
    id: "model-at-a-glance",
    title: "Model at a glance",
  },
  {
    id: "example-input-and-output",
    title: "Example input and output",
  },
  {
    id: "quickstart",
    title: "Quickstart with Nouli CLI",
  },
  {
    id: "provenance",
    title: "Base models",
  },
  {
    id: "limitations",
    title: "Limitations",
  },
  {
    id: "license-and-citation",
    title: "License and citation",
  },
];
const section = sectionLookup(sections);
---

<ModelLayout slug="nouli-policy-pair" sections={sections}>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p>
      Evaluate a written policy against the facts of a case. A policy extractor and evidence model
      work with Nouli to return TRUE, FALSE or UNKNOWN.
    </p>
    <p class="release-scope">
      Research preview, evaluated on bounded synthetic policies and narratives. The full pair
      requires the documented CUDA setup.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
  <ModelSection {...section("how-they-work-together")}>
    <p>
      <img
        src="/models/nouli-policy-pair/how-it-works.svg"
        alt="Policy flows through the extractor; information flows through the evidence model; Nouli applies the rules and returns TRUE, FALSE or UNKNOWN."
      />
    </p>
    <p>
      The extractor turns the policy into executable rules. The evidence model checks which required
      facts the supplied information supports. Nouli applies the rules, including calculations and
      comparisons, to reach the decision.
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("model-at-a-glance")}>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Property</th>
          <th>Value</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Input</td>
          <td>Policy text, case narrative and a query</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Output</td>
          <td>TRUE, FALSE or UNKNOWN</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Components</td>
          <td>Policy extractor and evidence model</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Tested full-pair runtime</td>
          <td>DGX Spark / Linux ARM64 / CUDA</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Inference</td>
          <td>Local; no hosted API key required</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>License</td>
          <td>Apache-2.0; upstream notices apply</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("example-input-and-output")}>
    <p>
      <strong>Input</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Policy:</strong> The taxpayer qualifies if the taxpayer is at least 65 years old on
      December 31 of the tax year.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Story:</strong> Mira was born on April 14, 1950.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Query:</strong> taxpayer <code>Mira</code>, other person <code>Tomas</code>, tax year{" "}
      <code>2025</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Recorded output</strong> (using the bundled policy program; trace fields omitted):
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      label="Recorded output"
      code={`{
  "status": "completed",
  "decision": "true"
}
`}
    />
    <p>
      Mira is 75 at the end of 2025, so she meets the policy's age requirement.{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-policy-pair/resolve/7de8e7f56085068f9cc380be829455b197300ebe/inference/examples/age-eligibility-story.txt">
        Example story
      </a>{" "}
      ·{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-policy-pair/resolve/7de8e7f56085068f9cc380be829455b197300ebe/inference/examples/age-eligibility-query.json">
        Query
      </a>{" "}
      ·{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-policy-pair/resolve/7de8e7f56085068f9cc380be829455b197300ebe/inference/examples/age-eligibility-output.json">
        Output excerpt
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("quickstart")}>
    <p>
      Requires Python 3.10 or newer, the{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/docs/huggingface_hub/guides/cli">HF CLI</a>, and the
      documented CUDA environment. The supplied bootstrap pins Nouli CLI 0.5.1. Public base weights
      are downloaded separately during setup.
    </p>
    <p>Download the complete repository:</p>
    <CodeBlock
      label="Terminal"
      code={`hf download nouli-ai/nouli-policy-pair --revision 7de8e7f56085068f9cc380be829455b197300ebe --local-dir ./nouli-policy-pair
cd nouli-policy-pair
`}
    />
    <p>
      Complete the{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-policy-pair/resolve/7de8e7f56085068f9cc380be829455b197300ebe/GETTING_STARTED.html">
        runtime setup
      </a>
      : build the native tools, open the pinned CUDA container, install dependencies, fetch the
      bases and generate <code>inference/local/config.json</code>.
    </p>
    <p>Then run the bundled example from the prepared runtime:</p>
    <CodeBlock
      label="Terminal"
      code={`.live-venv/bin/python inference/live_pair.py \\
  --config inference/local/config.json --device cuda \\
  --policy inference/examples/policy.txt \\
  --story inference/examples/age-eligibility-story.txt \\
  --taxpayer 'Mira' --other 'Tomas' --tax-year 2025 \\
  --output outputs/live.json
`}
    />
    <p>
      Read <code>outputs/live.json</code> for the decision. To evaluate your own case, replace the
      policy, story and query values. The setup guide also covers B-only execution with a saved
      program and offline reuse.
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("provenance")}>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507">Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya">convaiinnovations/laya</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This repository includes the selected extractor adapter and evidence-model delta with their
      custom runtime. Keep the complete download together and follow the supplied loader
      instructions.
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("limitations")}>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Evaluated on bounded synthetic policies and narratives. Real-world tax eligibility is
        unvalidated.
      </li>
      <li>
        Policy interpretation and evidence checks can make errors. Missing or unsupported facts can
        produce UNKNOWN.
      </li>
      <li>
        Full-pair use requires the documented CUDA setup. A clean installation on unrelated hardware
        remains unverified.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </ModelSection>
  <ModelSection {...section("license-and-citation")}>
    <p>
      Apache-2.0, with upstream notices retained in{" "}
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/nouli-ai/nouli-policy-pair/resolve/7de8e7f56085068f9cc380be829455b197300ebe/NOTICE">
        NOTICE
      </a>{" "}
      and <code>inference/licenses/</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://nouli.ai">Nouli AI</a>. Nouli Policy Pair. Cite the published model version
      and commit.
    </p>
  </ModelSection>
</ModelLayout>
